# Keeps the build context small and the builds reproducible.
#
# Every service Dockerfile uses `context: .` (the repository root) because the Maven reactor needs the
# root pom and the sibling modules a service depends on. That means `COPY . .` would otherwise drag
# in ~845 MB of local build output — 556 MB of node_modules alone — on every image build.
#
# Correctness matters more than speed here: a HOST `target/` copied into the builder can shadow what
# the in-image `mvn package` produces, so a stale local artifact silently becomes the shipped one.
# Excluding it forces the image to build from source.

# Local build output. Rebuilt inside the image.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
ui/review-web/dist/

# Secrets. Compose supplies environment at RUN time; the image must never contain the key.
.env
.env.backup-*

# VCS and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
**/*.iml

# OS metadata
**/.DS_Store

# Logs and scratch
*.log

# Docs and fixtures are not needed to compile a service. `demo/` is mounted or uploaded at runtime,
# not baked in.
demo/
README.md
